---
const { contactEmail } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of the NYC Jobs mobile application, listed in
      some stores as NYC Government Job Tracker (the "App" or "Service"), provided by Restart Apps.
      By downloading, accessing, or using the App, you agree to these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Purpose of the App</h2>
    <p>
      The App is designed to help users browse NYC government job listings, save jobs and searches,
      create local job alerts and reminders, review hiring insights, and access official application
      pages. The App retrieves posting data from NYC Open Data and provides shortcuts to official
      CityJobs pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App is an independent application. It is not an official City of New York application and
      is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the City of New York.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Eligibility and Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the App only for lawful purposes and in compliance with applicable laws,
      regulations, and platform rules. You agree not to misuse the App, interfere with its normal
      operation, attempt unauthorized access, reverse engineer the App except where permitted by
      law, or use the App in a way that could damage the Service or other users.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Job Information and Official Applications</h2>
    <p>
      Job listings, salaries, requirements, deadlines, agency information, and other
      employment-related details are provided for convenience and informational purposes only. We do
      not guarantee that any listing or detail is complete, current, accurate, or still available.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for verifying all job information, deadlines, and eligibility requirements
      through CityJobs before relying on that information or submitting an application. Official
      CityJobs information is available at: <a href="https://cityjobs.nyc.gov/jobs" target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">https://cityjobs.nyc.gov/jobs</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Alerts, Notifications, and Saved Content</h2>
    <p>
      The App may let you save jobs, save searches, and create local job alerts. Alerts and
      notifications are provided as a convenience only. We do not guarantee that alerts will be sent
      on time, delivered successfully, or include every relevant opening.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for monitoring official sources for application deadlines and updates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Accounts and Authentication</h2>
    <p>
      Certain personalization features may rely on Google Sign-In, Sign in with Apple, and Firebase
      Authentication. If you choose to sign in, you are responsible for maintaining the security of
      your device and your sign-in account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>NYCJobs Pro and In-App Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      The App may offer NYCJobs Pro as a one-time, non-subscription in-app purchase. The features,
      limits, and price presented on the purchase screen apply at the time of purchase. Purchases
      and restorations are processed by Google Play or Apple's App Store and remain subject to the
      applicable store account, payment, refund, and platform terms. We do not directly process
      payment-card information or control app-store refund decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for using the correct store account when purchasing or restoring Pro.
      Deleting your App account does not automatically refund, cancel, or erase a purchase
      maintained by an app store.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Third-Party Services and Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The App relies on third-party services, including NYC Open Data, Google Sign-In, Sign in with
      Apple, Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Firebase Cloud Storage, Firebase App Check,
      Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, Firebase Performance Monitoring, mapping and
      location services, Google Play Billing or Apple StoreKit, and, if enabled, Google AdMob and
      related consent tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      If advertising is enabled in the version of the App you use, ads may be served by Google AdMob
      or its partners. We are not responsible for third-party services, websites, ad content, or
      privacy practices, and your use of those services may be subject to separate terms and
      policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      The App's design, code, branding, and original content are protected by applicable
      intellectual property laws. Government job data, agency names, trademarks, and related
      materials remain the property of their respective owners.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The App is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
      purpose, non-infringement, availability, or accuracy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental,
      special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits,
      opportunities, or employment prospects arising out of or related to your use of the App.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Animation Credit</h2>
    <p>
      The Pro animation, "Businessman flies up with rocket" by Abdul Latif, is provided through
      LottieFiles under the Lottie Simple License: <a href="https://lottiefiles.com/page/license"
      target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://lottiefiles.com/page/license</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will update the effective date
      shown above. By continuing to use the App after updated Terms take effect, you agree to the
      revised Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about these Terms, contact us at: <a
      href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
